From: Li Guan <guanli.oerv@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] build: Avoid the dynamic percent-n probe on glibc

The legacy snprintf length probe uses a writable format containing %n,
which hardened glibc rejects at runtime.  Use the fallback formatter on
glibc while retaining the existing path elsewhere.

Signed-off-by: Li Guan <guanli.oerv@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
---
diff --git a/lib/vasnprintf.c b/lib/vasnprintf.c
--- a/lib/vasnprintf.c
+++ b/lib/vasnprintf.c
@@ -88 +88,6 @@
-# define USE_SNPRINTF 1
+# if defined __GLIBC__
+/* glibc rejects the writable format used for the %n length probe. */
+#  define USE_SNPRINTF 0
+# else
+#  define USE_SNPRINTF 1
+# endif
@@ -103 +108,6 @@
-# define USE_SNPRINTF (HAVE_DECL__SNPRINTF || HAVE_SNPRINTF)
+# if defined __GLIBC__
+/* glibc rejects the writable format used for the %n length probe. */
+#  define USE_SNPRINTF 0
+# else
+#  define USE_SNPRINTF (HAVE_DECL__SNPRINTF || HAVE_SNPRINTF)
+# endif
